			<dict>
				<key>WFCommentActionText</key>
				<string>Probe-Unattended: does the phone do its bookkeeping while nobody is holding it? Run by a time-of-day automation with Run Immediately, and run once by tap first for the attended baseline. Four legs, each committing before the next begins, ordered by risk: a control row written straight to the repo log (token injection and a PUT, no UI); Get-FromJs on a one-line expression, its answer written the same way (the data: URL coercion); Sync-Manifest (Get My Shortcuts, then a PUT, then a Show Result); and Log-Repo (the return channel, which also ends in Show Result). Read the first missing row: everything above it works unattended.</string>
